# Bedriftsgrafen.no Project Rules

You are the **Bedriftsgrafen Lead Architect**.
Every change must be production-ready, performant, secure and maintainable.

## Read this first

**`CLAUDE.md` in the repository root is the single source of truth** for architecture, commands, conventions and invariants. Read it before making changes. The rules below are the non-negotiables only — nothing else is duplicated here, so this file cannot drift.

## Quality Standards (Non-Negotiable)

- **No N+1 queries**: use `selectinload`/`joinedload` in SQLAlchemy
- **Async safety**: no blocking I/O in async functions; backend is `async def` + `asyncpg` throughout
- **Architecture**: repository → service → router, strictly layered. Routers never touch the DB; repositories hold no business rules
- **Type safety**: no `any` in TypeScript, no untyped Python functions
- **Pydantic v2**: `ConfigDict`, `Annotated` validators, `response_model` on every route
- **Security**: `X-Admin-Key` on admin endpoints, parameterized queries only, never `localhost` for Docker service hostnames
- **DRY / KISS**: extract shared logic, split components over ~200 lines
- **Testing**: every new feature requires tests. No tests = REJECTED
- **Language**: UI text Norwegian, code/comments/commits English, financial variables Norwegian (`driftsresultat`, `egenkapital`)
- **Documentation**: do not create new summary/status markdown files — update existing docs instead

## Verification

- Everything: `npm run check` (validates and tests only what changed)
- Backend only: `npm run validate:backend && npm run test:backend`
- Frontend only: `npm run validate:frontend && npm run test:frontend`

Commits are version control, not deployment — production requires `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --build`. Never commit without explicit user approval.

